    "text": "Calculate the compressional force required to prevent the metallic rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math> and cross-sectional area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>when heated through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, from expanding lengthwise. Young's modulus of elasticity of the metal is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> and mean coefficient of linear expansion is <math> <mrow> <mi>α</mi> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;per degree celsius.",
